ORDER BY: Sorts the result set in ascending (ASC, default) or descending (DESC) order based on one or more columns.
Example: SELECT * FROM Students ORDER BY Marks DESC;

HAVING: Filters groups created by GROUP BY based on an aggregate condition. It is similar to WHERE but operates on groups, not individual rows.
Example: SELECT Department, COUNT(*) FROM Employee GROUP BY Department HAVING COUNT(*) > 5;

